Z||000020||tgowens||07-22-2000||02:15 AM||||I have found help and given help on this forum and I have become a regular reader/writer on this forum.<P>This forum serves people from all over the world -- it is the one place that we can inquire about, tell about, complain about and laugh about the Fiero - and hopefully we will find others who have felt much the same as we do. Oh, there are some who get opinionated and some who feel that theirs is the only <I>right</I> way but they are the exceptions.<P>All in all, the members here are fun, knowledgeable, and - the beauty of it is, there is <I>no</I> generation gap - from the mid teens to the sixties -- all with a commonality -- what better place to be than Pennock's Forum -- Cliff, a <B>BIG</B> thank you from me!!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">                <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A><p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 07-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||2birds||07-22-2000||11:43 AM||||I wonder how I made it through the first 11 years of owning a fiero without this place.  It rules.||||reg||1
Z||000022||bHooper||07-22-2000||03:38 PM||||if it wasn't for this forum... i probably would not have been able to get my GT running.  i learned a whole lot about tranny's that i couldn't have learned other wise.<P>also the forum has given me the confidence, but not the cash  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, to go even further and swap engines... to the 3.4l, on my own.<P>thanks to everyone... you know who you are!<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000023||88formula||07-23-2000||11:24 AM||||If it weren’t for this forum I would have never considered performing the 3.4 swap I am doing now. I got a ton of feedback from you people on this forum and over the telephone. <P>I also like the quality of the people here as well. If you go to other forums like some F-body forums you find people in childish quarrels posting messages and things that I have never seen on this forum before. The people here are honest, professional, and civilized with an intrinsic interest in helping people make their cars better.<P>This place has the best source of information I have found anywhere about the Fiero. I have found more information about this car here than I ever could have anywhere else.<P>Thank you everyone and Cliff too.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 07-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||RobertVol||07-23-2000||11:44 AM||||Well Bi - Fiero Disorder = owning 2 <BR>Tri - Fiero Disorder would be = owning 3<P>And if you get up to seven your just a <BR>Fiero Sicky !!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>I wish I could be that sick ! <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT T top 55k for sale<BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>  <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/3eab6a20.jpg"> ||||reg||1
